# 2. Method

* **Storage.** NumPy/pandas for analysis. SQLite holds the untouched raw table, a working table with `role`, `in_primary`, `target` and `split` columns filled by SQL `UPDATE`, a `type_mapping` table, and a `primary_events` view that is exactly the modelling subset; everything was read back and verified against pandas.
* **Leakage control.** `type`, the index column and all identifiers are never predictors. Scaling and class weighting are fitted on training rows only. Hyper-parameters (including whether to use class weighting) are chosen by validation ROC-AUC; the operating threshold uses validation data only; validation and test data are never resampled, weighted or balanced; the test set is only scored.
* **Models.** Baselines: majority class (0 features; always predicts signal) and a single-feature cut that uses **one** feature, `{{single_feature}}`, picked as the best of {{n_candidates}} candidates by training AUC, with the cut maximising training *balanced* accuracy. Learned: logistic regression, decision tree, random forest, HistGradientBoosting; bounded random/grid searches (8-12 configurations).
* **Class weighting.** `class_weight` (training-only) is a tuned option for every learned model; the validation comparison is in Table F.
* **Metrics.** Class 1 = signal. *Signal efficiency* = fraction of true signal retained; *continuum rejection* = fraction of true continuum rejected; *continuum acceptance* = fraction of true continuum wrongly kept = 1 - rejection. Also accuracy, signal precision/recall/F1, balanced accuracy, macro-F1 and per-class precision/recall/F1.
* **Uncertainty.** Efficiency and rejection use exact (Clopper-Pearson) 95% intervals with their actual denominators ({{test_sig}} signal, {{test_con}} continuum). ROC-AUC uses a stratified bootstrap (signal and continuum resampled separately, 1,000 resamples). Model comparisons use a paired stratified bootstrap on the shared test rows. All of these treat the fitted models as fixed and cannot capture training-set variability, which is large with {{train_con}} training continuum events; {{n_splits_extra}} further re-splits with frozen hyper-parameters give an extra view.
* **Feature reduction.** (1) correlation filter (|Spearman| >= {{corr_thr}} on training rows, keep the more separating feature): {{n_feat}} -> {{n_corr}}; (2) rank by permutation importance of a class-weighted gradient-boosting model on validation data; (3) {{crit}}: k = {{k_sel}}. All learned models were re-tuned and evaluated with the same protocol.

